                <pb facs="1037" n="921" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg921"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.6463/110: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-16T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>14. Reference Welles’ 47, April 12, 11 a.m.</p>
                <p>Department would be very glad if Provisional Government and representatives
                    San[to] Domingo Water, Light and Power Company can make a mutually satisfactory
                    agreement <hi rendition="#italic">ad referendum</hi> for the purchase of the
                    Company’s properties by the municipalities of Santiago and Puerto Plata.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
